  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rLocation Plan 09.02.2026\rProposed Site Block Plan AP100 Dec 2025\rExisting Floor Plans AE101 Dec 2025\rExisting Section AE201 Dec 2025\rExisting Elevations AE301 Dec 2025\rExisting 3D View AE901 Dec 2025\rProposed Floor Plans AP101 Dec 2025\rProposed Section AP201 Dec 2025\rProposed Elevations AP301 Dec 2025\rProposed 3D View AP901 Dec 2025\rPlanning Statement \rNoise Impact Assessment Rev. 1.0 Dated 15.01.2026\rOdour Risk Assessment Rev. 1.0 Dated 15.01.2026\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Prior to first use of the flue, the noise control system as contained within the Noise Impact Assessment Report must be installed and permanently retained for the lifetime of the development.\r\rReason: To protect the local amenity from noise\r",
    "All new external work shall be carried out in materials that resemble, as closely as possible, in colour and texture as specified in the approved application.\r\rReason: To safeguard the appearance of the premises and the character of the immediate area.\r",
    "No plant or equipment shall be affixed to any external face of a building or added to the roof of a building other than that shown in the approved drawings.\r\rReason: In the interest of amenity and to ensure a satisfactory external appearance in accordance with policy D4 of the London Plan (2021), CP30 of the Enfield Core Strategy (2010) and DMD37 of the Enfield Development Management Policy (2014).\r",
    "Before the use of the flue hereby permitted takes place, equipment to control the emission of fumes and smell from the premises shall be installed in accordance with a scheme to be first submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. All equipment installed as part of the approved scheme shall thereafter be operated and maintained in accordance with that approval and retained for so long as the use continues.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenities of the occupiers of nearby residential properties.\r",
    "The plant shall be supported on adequate proprietary anti-vibration mounts as necessary to prevent the structural transmission of vibration and regenerated noise within adjacent or adjoining premises, and these shall be so maintained thereafter.\r\rReason: To safeguard the amenities of the occupiers of nearby residential properties.\r"
  ],
